    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d539-a1">

                <pb facs="0670" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg556"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Telegram]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tsao Kun</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Coolidge</hi><anchor
                        n="89" xml:id="d539-f1"/></head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President</hi>: I consider it a privilege to
                    bespeak, on behalf of my fellow citizens, to Your Excellency and the people of
                    the United States our sincere appreciation of the generosity shown in the
                    remission of their portion of the 1901 indemnity. The remission of a part of
                    this indemnity in 1908 contributed much to the special friendliness toward the
                    people of the United States, which had developed in the hearts of the Chinese
                    people ever since the beginning of intercourse between our two peoples. The
                    present action will still further increase the friendliness, and Your
                    Excellency’s Government have thus placed the people of China under an endless
                    debt of gratitude to the people of the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsao Kun</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d539-f1" n="89" type="source" xml:id="d539-f1-content">
                <p>Acknowledgment of this message was transmitted in telegram no. 134, June 28,
                    1924, to the Minister in China (file no. 493.11/1045a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
